================================================================================================================================

# 28. DELETE SAFETY RULES

================================================================================================================================

The following rules are mandatory:

```text
1. Never delete broker executions through Manual Delete.

2. Partial Exit deletion uses exact execution_id.

3. Complete lifecycle deletion uses contract_key.

4. Every deletion is scoped to the authenticated user.

5. User identity comes from server-side authentication.

6. MANUAL- lifecycle protection remains enforced.

7. Zero matching rows is an error.

8. Do not manually restore quantities after deleting exits.

9. Let pairTrades() reconstruct the resulting state.

10. Never delete reconstructed trades as the canonical operation.

11. Do not create a second FIFO engine.
```

================================================================================================================================

# 29. RELATIONSHIP TO ATOMIC EDIT

================================================================================================================================

Atomic Edit and Atomic Delete are separate persistence operations.

### Atomic Edit

```text
DELETE old
+
INSERT corrected
=
ONE ATOMIC REPLACEMENT
```

### Atomic Delete

```text
DELETE targeted execution/lifecycle
=
ONE SERVER-SIDE DESTRUCTIVE OPERATION
```

Both share the same architectural principles:

```text
Authenticated user
        ↓
Server API
        ↓
Server helper
        ↓
Privileged RPC
        ↓
Canonical executions
```

Neither operation directly modifies derived trades.

================================================================================================================================

# 30. RELATIONSHIP TO SERVER-SIDE VALIDATION

================================================================================================================================

Feature #27 established:

```text
lib/server/trades/validateManualExecutions.ts
```

for Manual execution replacement.

Atomic Delete has its own targeted validation because it receives a delete target rather than a new execution set.

The two validation boundaries are therefore intentionally different.

Do not force execution-set validation into a delete operation where it provides no value.

